<p>China’s annual “two sessions” political meetings begin in Beijing this week, starting with the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, followed shortly by the National People’s Congress (NPC), which is set to endorse the budget and major policy priorities. Ahead of the opening, NPC spokesman Lou Qinjian said Beijing wants a more resilient economy, but will not compromise on what it calls core principles in dealing with the United States. The gatherings are a closely watched guide to how the world’s second-largest economy plans to pursue growth while managing strains such as a property downturn—and how firmly it will back high-tech development, including artificial intelligence. Observers are also looking for near-term targets and spending signals—especially around technology and defense—that can shape expectations for policy direction and government outlays.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/IALAkQs-qFnmL_EGv3uI54KAhAD1v6JnAyeasTky893CMX3KBLXa3iagvzogtyA-LREjM1sfMzdrDOjjPBqHI-kVJsO16R99yZJcUoXq9uxMhNKV-Ds435Ylt2r5KlNb6gPX-FXHwXoWRNd4AWwUrVGoeWYuZ5V-zIyjLmaLgu142cWy4mDoEbiPMsdKQnUqRd4Km22DoJGmWayjEFg_r_uLew' alt='Delegates arrive in Beijing ahead of China’s annual parliamentary session.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Who attends: Thousands of delegates from mainland China, Hong Kong and Macau travel to Beijing for the meetings, which ratify legislation, budgets and personnel decisions over about two weeks.</li><li>Five-year focus: Chinese leaders use the NPC to set policy and economic goals and to sketch priorities for the years ahead, including longer-range planning tied to five-year goals.</li><li>Political backdrop: As delegates gather, attention is also on internal security politics, with reports noting more Chinese military generals being purged ahead of the meetings.</li><li>Defense signals: The meetings are expected to approve China’s defense budget and outline related security priorities as part of the annual package of targets and spending plans.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lou Qinjian (NPC spokesman): Lou said China aims to strengthen economic resilience while sticking to its core principles in dealings with the United States. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3345464/china-vows-boost-economy-adhere-principles-ahead-two-sessions-and-trump-visit'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Chinese government (NPC agenda): Officials said China wants to keep communication open with Washington while holding to its stated “red lines,” and that the NPC session is expected to unveil the year’s economic targets and policy priorities. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/china-says-it-seeks-communicationswith-us-but-vows-to-hold-its-red-lines/article70702270.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>BBC explainer analysis: The BBC says the meetings are carefully choreographed, but still closely watched for signals on economic priorities, technology and the broader direction of governance. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2lrxyke7kro'>BBC</a>)</li><li>PBS/Reuters analysis: PBS reports that China’s high-tech ambitions are running up against slower growth and other economic realities, shaping what policymakers can credibly deliver this year. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinas-economic-ambitions-hit-limits-to-growth-as-its-national-congress-prepares-to-meet'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3345464/china-vows-boost-economy-adhere-principles-ahead-two-sessions-and-trump-visit'>China vows to boost economy, adhere to principles ahead of ‘two sessions’ and Trump visit</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/china-says-it-seeks-communicationswith-us-but-vows-to-hold-its-red-lines/article70702270.ece'>China says it seeks communications with U.S. but vows to hold its ‘red lines’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/china-unveil-priorities-coming-5-years-major-annual-130734358'>China to unveil priorities for coming 5 years at major annual political meeting</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/china-to-kick-off-two-sessions-conclave-today-to-rubber-stamp-xis-economic-defence-plans-13986079.html'>China to kick off ‘two sessions’ conclave today to rubber stamp Xi’s economic &amp; defence plans</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/04/china-two-sessions-2026-meeting-what-are-they-when-is-it-explainer'>China’s Two Sessions: what are the meetings and why do they matter?</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2lrxyke7kro'>What to know about the &#x27;two sessions&#x27;,  China&#x27;s biggest political meeting</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinas-economic-ambitions-hit-limits-to-growth-as-its-national-congress-prepares-to-meet'>China&#x27;s economic ambitions hit limits to growth as its national congress prepares to meet</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>